message: >-
  Please cite this research package using the metadata below. The manuscript
  identifies Alexander Filin as project coordinator and describes the human
  and AI contributions in its contribution statement.
title: "Pure S Is Computationally Universal Under a Fixed Root-Restarted Finite Controller"
type: software
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-09-14
repository-code: "https://github.com/cstrawberry/predictive-universe/tree/main/docs/paper/related/pure_s_universality"
authors:
  - name: "Cinematic Strawberry"
contact:
  - given-names: "Alexander"
    family-names: "Filin"
    email: "contact@cinematicstrawberry.com"
abstract: >-
  Pure S is computationally universal under one fixed finite controller
  restarted at the root after each contraction. Only the bare term is retained
  between invocations. On every finite term the controller terminates within
  a linear microtick bound and performs exactly one contextual S contraction
  or reports normality without mutation. Every encoded cyclic-tag input has
  the exact certified trajectory, with all other samples rejected. The fixed
  period-912 specialization supplies a complete effective padded tape encoder,
  literal source rows and terminal scanned-bit output, with measured interface
  bounds. Supporting theorems characterize confluence limits and
  permanence of verified histories along every reduction, cofinal recovery,
  and complete enumeration along one address-complete path in the unrestricted
  graph; the observer checks the source transition relation on supplied rows.
keywords:
  - combinatory logic
  - S combinator
  - term rewriting
  - root-restarted finite controller
  - exact checkpoint decoder
  - literal source output
  - observer-verified history enumeration
  - formal verification
  - universal computation
